## AI Agent Reasoning

### Context
Issue #26 fixes CxxTest compilation failures caused by generated declarations
for a submitted C++ main conflicting with CxxTest's runner main.

### Decisions Made
- Preserve legacy fixtures that include program.cpp themselves, avoiding
  duplicate definitions.
- Use a harness mode for fixtures without that include, so tests can call one
  no-argument program_main wrapper for supported main signatures.
- Exclude main from generated declarations rather than broadening the existing
  limited declaration regex into a C++ parser.

### Trade-off
Argument-taking main is invoked with argc 0 and argv nullptr. This supports
entry-point testing without expanding the public execute API to carry argv.

### Verification
Docker CxxTest smoke tests cover no-argument, void, named and unnamed argc/argv,
array argv, and legacy fixture forms.
